  "name": "Create MiniMax Hailuo videos and auto post to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "55b21523-79a7-48e8-a9ab-d0daabb01940",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -633,
        -97
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 812,
        "content": "## Create MiniMax Hailuo videos from a list of ideas and post them\nTurn video ideas from Google Sheets into MiniMax Hailuo clips: every day MiniMax writes the shot, renders a vertical video and PostWire posts it to TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts with a caption for each network.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every day at 10:00** reads the rows marked ready. **Take the next idea** picks the first one and **Mark the idea as generating** claims it, so a clip is never paid for twice.\n2. **Write the video prompt** (MiniMax) returns the shot description, a caption idea and the YouTube title.\n3. **Hailuo render** (MiniMax) generates the clip in 9:16 and waits until it is ready.\n4. **Post to TikTok, Reels and Shorts** (PostWire) uploads the file, writes a caption per network and publishes.\n5. **Mark the idea as posted** writes the post links in the row. When the render or a network fails, **Write the fix in the row** and **Email me the fix** tell you what to fix.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Add a MiniMax credential to both MiniMax nodes. One API key covers text and video; video is billed per clip.\n3. Create a sheet with the columns idea, style, status, posted_at, links and note. Write ready in status to queue an idea, and pick the sheet in the four Sheets nodes.\n4. Connect Gmail and fill in **Channel settings**.\n\n### Customize\nChange the model or length in the Hailuo render node, the style in Channel settings, or the networks in the PostWire node (the free plan posts to 2 networks per post)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
